{
  "dom_id": "step-q555464",
  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the best estimate for $\\sqrt{55}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To estimate $\\sqrt{55},$ we first find the two perfect squares closest to $55.$\n\nThe closest perfect squares are $49={7}^{2}$ and $64={8}^{2}.$\n\nSince $49<55<64,$ we know that the square root of $55$ lies between $7$ and $8.$ This tells us that $6.8$ and $27.5$ are incorrect estimates.\n\nBecause $55$ is slightly closer to $49$ than to $64$ (the distance to $49$ is $6,$ and the distance to $64$ is $9$), we expect $\\sqrt{55}$ to be near the middle, but slightly less than $7.5.$ \n\nWe can test the plausible choices by squaring them to see which one results in a value closest to $55:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7.1}^{2} & =50.41 \\\\ {7.4}^{2} & =54.76 \\\\ {7.9}^{2} & =62.41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that ${7.4}^{2}=54.76$ is very close to $55.$ \n\nTherefore, the best estimate for $\\sqrt{55}$ is $7.4.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
